    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. but it feels like more than just a creative block. it's like i'm just waiting for a way to make the feeling stop for good. i was reading about how some artists believe that the only way to achieve something truly raw and honest is to fully embrace the darkness, even if it means losing yourself in it. like, maybe the most honest thing a person can do is just... stop trying to fight the emptiness. does that make any sense artistically?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
