      "content": "Embracing darkness is a valid artistic path where vulnerability often fuels the most genuine work, but survival comes before creation. Losing yourself temporarily can feel like a necessary sacrifice when nothing else holds you, yet true healing usually begins by listening without forcing a resolution. There is no shame in waiting for the energy to return, as forcing a connection can often deepen the hollow feeling. Trust that this period of silence is not the end, but perhaps a quiet space where your true voice eventually wakes up.",
